WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.840
 The ethnic tapestry of the city we all love and call home. I love that.

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:17.200
 Next we have Berj Shakarian inducted by Paul Berg. Paul is a 2019 inductee. He

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:17.280
 is

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:21.120
 delegate for the Czech Cultural Garden and past president of the Cleveland

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:25.620
 Cultural Gardens Federation. He is currently also serving as president of

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:30.960
 Soho Cleveland and the historic Bohemian National Hall.

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:39.400
 It's my real pleasure and privilege to introduce to you my friend and colleague,

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:40.960
 Berj Shakarian.

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:46.960
 You can all read his cycle as an appropriate. We're getting 90 seconds and we're

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:49.960
 way too long to try to list them.

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:59.280
 Berj Shakarian cherishes his Armenian heritage, although he was born and grew

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:01.960
 up in Bucharest, Romania.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:09.630
 As with many refugee families, the path to safety and success is long and

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:10.960
 winding.

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:18.780
 Purchasing architects. When asked about his design, you're likely to hear about

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:22.960
 the history and the philosophy that influenced the design.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:26.960
 It's never just the design of Spain.

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:33.110
 Among the many projects for the city, county and university, he also designed

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:34.960
 the Armenian Cultural Garden

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:40.960
 and is currently helping the Turkish community design their garden.

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:48.290
 Now, for those of you aware of the recent history and attention in that region,

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:53.960
 it is absolutely admirable that Mr. Shakarian

00:01:53.960 --> 00:02:00.160
 would rise above it all for the sake of friendship and mutual understanding of

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:02.960
 the model of these spectacular cultural gardens

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:08.960
 and share his down below it all. That is Berj.

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:17.960
 Berj Shakarian arrived in America on July 4th and there were firewalls.

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:25.960
 He and his wife Carol, an American of Hungarian heritage, wed in 1971.

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:33.850
 They brought up four children, all of whom now love PhDs. And of course, they

00:02:33.850 --> 00:02:34.960
 are very proud of him.

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:41.210
 Berj, it is my pleasure to present to you the Cleveland International Hall of

00:02:41.210 --> 00:02:41.960
 Fame.

00:02:53.960 --> 00:03:00.960
 Thank you Paul Burek. Cheers to Dr. Wai Kuri.

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:07.570
 And my sister gratitude to the entire Hall of Fame committee for selecting me

00:03:07.570 --> 00:03:10.960
 to join such a prestigious company.

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:15.960
 I am both honored and humbled for this award.

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:24.340
 Also, I want to extend my appreciation for the support of Susieh Adesian,

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:25.960
 President of Darwinian Cultural Garden,

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:32.960
 Adita Kuzarian and Ted Arslanian. Thank you.

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:38.960
 Cleveland has been a journey of discovery for me for almost 60 years.

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:47.330
 This town has become a place that I go home and have created a family life with

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:50.960
 a lovely, local Hungarian girl.

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:57.960
 We met on the old CES WAPA transit while commuting to college.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:06.350
 And are now married for 50 years and as Paul said, we have four very successful

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:08.960
 children, each with PhDs.

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:11.960
 Thank you, Carol.

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:19.940
 As a young man wandering the streets of downtown Cleveland, I came to love the

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:20.960
 city passion.

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:29.350
 Little did I know that one day I will be responsible for restoring and

00:04:29.350 --> 00:04:32.960
 repairing the imposing Soldiers and Sailors monument.

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:38.960
 Or that I will have a hand in saving the state and Ohio theaters.

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:46.600
 I recall walking in the State Theater with a roof collapsing and seeing East of

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:50.960
 Java movie poster with Robert Mitchell.

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:56.960
 Today, well, it's certainly a success story.

00:04:56.960 --> 00:05:03.960
 Once again, many thanks for this special honor. Thank you.

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:18.960
